extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 printed 157-159 (cache p157-p159, page_offset 0). The lore is 157, Modify Machines runs 157-158, the device list, powers, gizmos, I.S.P. and the start of the skills 158, the related list, secondary skills, equipment, money and cybernetics 159. No gizmoteer class was in production on 2026-09-25. || CATEGORY: headed Gizmoteer R.C.C. but stored as an O.C.C. The skills are printed O.C.C. Skills / O.C.C. Related Skills, the Amaki R.C.C. (155) lists the Gizmoteer among its common O.C.C.s, the lore says gizmoteers are found in every Amaki House as designers and troubleshooters, and printed 152 says humans excel in the same field: a profession, not a species. It prints no attribute dice or pools. No race_restrictions. || XP: the Gizmoteer ladder on printed 192, as briefed. Level 11 prints 137,000, equal to level 10''s upper bound (every other band starts one above the previous end) - a book slip, stored AS PRINTED per the brief; strictly rising still holds (96901 < 137000 < 188101). || GROUP: psychic - a psionic whose whole occupation is its powers. No sdc_base or mdc_base; men_of_arms: false (no men-of-arms heading covers it; a technician and psychic). || PSIONICS: tier not printed; stored master because the picks reach the Super category under the Mind Melter''s limits, which only a master psionic can. Mind Block, Speed Reading, Total Recall, Electrokinesis and Telemechanics granted by name (the powers usable without a gizmo). ''Select two powers from all four categories'' read as two from EACH of Healing, Physical, Sensitive and Super (8 picks, four starting groups), since the next sentence contrasts it with ''two powers from any categories'' per level - judgement call. Every level after the first: two from any category (schedule 2-15). Mind Melter limits: Mind Wipe, Psi-Sword and Mentally Possess Others not before third level, as a Super except on the starting group and the level-2 entry. Gizmo-only use of the picks cannot be enforced; it is in each pick''s note and an ability. I.S.P. 2D4x10 + M.E., +2D6 per level. || ABILITIES: Modify Machines, the psionic TW device list, gizmo-only powers, 1D4+2 starting gizmos and TW savvy are special_abilities text; the magicians-pay-double-P.P.E. rule is in the device text. Starting gizmos have no catalog row and none is stubbed. || SKILLS: Language and Literacy: Amaki 98 as Language: Amaki + Literacy: Native Language (the Arkhon precedent). One language and literacy of choice (+20%) as a choose 1 of Language: Spanish or Language: Other and a choose 1 of Literacy: Other, both bonus 20. Radio: Basic 45+15; Advanced Math as Mathematics: Advanced 45+15; Basic Electronics 30+15; one Pilot of choice +10; W.P. Energy Pistol; W.P. Sword; Hand to Hand: Basic, to Expert for one other skill or Martial Arts for two (hand_to_hand costs). In an Amaki pairing Language: Amaki and the two W.P.s are held once. || RELATED: ten, at least four from Electrical or Mechanical (a union floor, minimums). Two more at levels 3 and 6, one at 8, 10 and 12. Communications +10, Domestic, Electrical +15, Espionage Intelligence and Wilderness Survival only (+5; Wilderness Survival is a Wilderness row, reachable because Wilderness is granted), Mechanical +15, Medical +5, Military +5, Physical, Pilot +5, Pilot Related +5, Rogue, Science +10, Technical +10, W.P., Wilderness. Secondary: five, same limits without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: a suit of body armor as a choice led by amaki-combat-armor and duelist-articulated-armor (the book allows Duelist armor) plus this book''s other armor rows; blast-sword; 4 spare E-clips; an energy or non-energy weapon from a catalog set; basic tool kit (tool-kit); miniature tool kit (mini-tool-kit); canteen; sleeping bag; two sets of dress clothing; one set of traveling clothing. || MONEY: 2D4x1000 credits. class-check warns that a race stating its own starting_money would win a pairing; the Amaki R.C.C. states none, so this applies with it, and the book does not make the class replace its race, so no supersedes_race. || CYBERNETICS: none to start, a restriction line."
